            <p class="CiteTOC"><a href="../Flagstaff01/Flagstaff0114000.html#1.14.001.0006.11">1-14-001-0006.11</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ATTENDANCE AND HOURS WORKED</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0001"><a name="1.14.001.0001">1-14-001-0001</a> PERSONNEL SYSTEM ADOPTED</h3>
            <p class="P0">There is hereby established pursuant to Article IV, section 5, of the Charter of the City a personnel system based on the principles of merit and fitness to be known as the &quot;Flagstaff Employee Handbook of Regulations,&quot; which may be amended from time to time, three (3) copies of which shall be kept on file in the office of the City Clerk and there retained available for the use and inspection by any interested person during normal business hours.</p>

            <p class="P0">Any person found in violation of a provision of the Flagstaff Employee Handbook of Regulations<span class="superscript">*</span> may be subject to discipline, as set forth in such handbook. (Ord. 2003-21, 11/08/2003; Ord. 2010-33, Amended, 11/09/2010; Ord. 2012-14, Amended, 10/02/2012; Ord. 2013-09, Amended, 05/07/2013; Ord. 2015-14, Amended, 09/01/2015; Ord. 2017-12, Amended, 05/16/2017; Ord. 2017-26, Amended, 09/19/2017; Ord. 2018-18, Amended, 05/15/2018; Ord. 2018-19, Amended, 06/04/2018; Ord. 2018-26, Amended, 08/21/2018; Ord. 2018-31, Amended, 09/04/2018; Ord. 2018-35, Amended, 11/06/2018; Ord. 2018-36, Amended, 11/06/2018; Ord. 2018-39, Amended, 12/11/2018; Ord. 2019-10, Amended, 06/02/2019; Ord. 2020-06, Amended, 03/17/2020; Ord. 2020-08, Amended, 05/05/2020; Ord. 2021-02, Amended, 03/02/2021; Ord. 2022-10, Amended, 05/03/2022; Ord. 2022-14, Amended, 06/21/2022; Ord. 2022-15, Amended, 07/05/2022; Ord. 2022-23, Amended, 09/20/2022; Ord. 2023-30, Amended, 12/19/2023; Ord. 2024-08, </p>

            <p class="P0">Amended, 03/19/2024; Ord. 2024-09, Amended, 04/16/2024; Ord. 2024-11, Amended, 04/16/2024; Ord. 2024-15, Amended, 05/21/2024; Ord. 2025-05, Amended, 04/15/2025 (Res. 2025-17); Ord. 2025-27, Amended, 11/18/2025; Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026; Ord. 2026-19, Amended, 08/25/2026)</p>

            <p class="Footnote">*Code reviser&rsquo;s note: The Employee Handbook is <a href="../FlagstaffEmployeeHandbook/FlagstaffEmployeeHandbook0110.html">available here</a>.</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0002"><a name="1.14.001.0002">1-14-001-0002</a> HUMAN RESOURCES DIRECTOR</h3>
            <p class="P0">The City Manager, or other such officer or employee as he may designate, shall be the Human Resources Director of the City and shall be charged with the proper and efficient administration and operation of the City of Flagstaff Personnel System.</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0003"><a name="1.14.001.0003">1-14-001-0003</a> APPLICABILITY OF RULES</h3>
            <p class="P0">Nothing in the rules or policies adopted for their implementation shall be construed or interpreted to reduce or restrict any powers or duties provided for in the Charter of the City.</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0004"><a name="1.14.001.0004">1-14-001-0004</a> RIGHTS OF CITY RETAINED</h3>
            <p class="P0">The City retains the exclusive right through the City Manager, subject to the provisions of the City Charter, applicable State law and the personnel regulations to:</p>

            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Direct and supervise its employees;</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Appoint, promote, classify, transfer, assign, retain, suspend, demote, discharge, or take disciplinary action against any employee;</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Relieve from duty any employee because of lack of funds, lack of work, reorganization or for any other legitimate reason;</p>

            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Maintain the efficiency of its governmental operations;</p>

            <p class="P1">E.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Determine the means, methods and personnel by which operations are to be conducted;</p>

            <p class="P1">F.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Take whatever actions may be necessary to carry out its responsibilities in situations of emergency. (Ord. 1116, 6-3-80)</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0005"><a name="1.14.001.0005">1-14-001-0005</a> CITY RETIREMENT SYSTEMS</h3>
            <p class="P0">The City hereby participates in and adheres to the policies and procedures, rules and regulations of the Arizona State Employees Retirement System and Plan and the Arizona Public Safety Personnel Retirement System, as said Systems and Plan are applicable to officers and employees of the City.<span class="Superscript">1</span> (1978 Code)</p>

            <p class="Footnote"><span class="Superscript">1</span>Charter Art. IV, sec. 4</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006"><a name="1.14.001.0006">1-14-001-0006</a> EMPLOYEE ADVISORY COMMITTEE</h3>
            <p class="P0">The Employee Advisory Committee (EAC) is hereby established. (Ord. 2014-32, Amended, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.1"><a name="1.14.001.0006.1">1-14-001-0006.1</a> Definitions</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&quot;Regular member&quot; is an eligible employee elected to serve on behalf of that employee&rsquo;s respective group.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&quot;Alternate member&quot; is an eligible employee elected to serve on the EAC when the regular member is unable to attend and will fulfill the regular member&rsquo;s term in the event of a vacancy.</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&quot;Eligible employee&quot; is any full-time or part-time tenured or exempt employee not identified as an &quot;ineligible employee.&quot;</p>

            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&quot;Ineligible employee&quot; is any appointed employee, Assistant City Manager, Deputy City Manager, Division Director (except as noted in Section <a href="../Flagstaff01/Flagstaff0114000.html#1.14.001.0006.5">1-14-001-0006.5</a>), Section Head, Deputy Human Resources Director, Human Resources/Risk Management Manager, probationary employee, or temporary employee. (Ord. 2010-33, Amended, 11/09/2010; Ord. 2014-32, Amended, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2024-11, Amended, 04/16/2024; Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.2"><a name="1.14.001.0006.2">1-14-001-0006.2</a> Mission Statement</h3>
            <p class="P0">The mission of the EAC is to serve as a body of elected members and alternates to represent individual employees, employee groups, and City divisions with fairness and impartiality. (Ord. 2014-32, Amended, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.3"><a name="1.14.001.0006.3">1-14-001-0006.3</a> Purpose</h3>
            <p class="P0">The purpose of the EAC is to foster ongoing employee-employer relations by providing a process and forum for employees to recommend changes to the City Manager concerning employment-related policies and procedures, safety, compensation, and benefits. The EAC does not make recommendations regarding the hiring, discipline, promotion, demotion, transfer, voluntary reassignment, suspension, or dismissal of individual employees.</p>

            <p class="P0">The EAC is established for the purpose of discussing and making recommendations based on requests received from individual employees, employee groups, and City Divisions with fairness and impartiality. The EAC is an advisory committee and does not represent individual employees regarding their own personal issues and/or an individual&rsquo;s personnel issues.</p>

            <p class="P0">Individual employment issues shall be processed through any of the City&rsquo;s established grievance or appeal procedures. Employees are encouraged to resolve any issue or employment-related concern through the established administrative procedures. (Ord. 2010-33, Amended, 11/09/2010; Ord. 2014-32, Amended, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2025-05, Amended, 04/15/2025 (Res. 2025-17); Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.4"><a name="1.14.001.0006.4">1-14-001-0006.4</a> Objectives</h3>
            <p class="P0">The objectives of the EAC are to:</p>

            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Work together in the spirit of trust and cooperation to reach consensus on matters under discussion and, in doing so, refrain from acting independently on behalf of the EAC without prior approval of a majority vote.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Review and recommend to the City Manager any initiatives or changes to City&rsquo;s policies and procedures related to employment, safety, compensation, or benefits prior to submission to the City Council for consideration.</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide a forum for employees to discuss City-wide employee issues as they pertain to employment-related policies and procedures, safety, compensation, and benefits.</p>

            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ensure that each member consistently attends EAC meetings and regularly communicates with the employees in their respective employee group.</p>

            <p class="P1">E.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Attend, participate in, and/or provide input and recommendations at City Council budget meetings.</p>

            <p class="P1">F.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Respond to City Manager questions or concerns. (Ord. 2010-33, Amended, 11/09/2010; Ord. 2014-32, Amended, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2025-05, Amended, 04/15/2025 (Res. 2025-17); Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.5"><a name="1.14.001.0006.5">1-14-001-0006.5</a> Structure</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Employee Advisory Committee shall consist of elected regular members and alternate members representing employee groups across the organization. Employee groups are determined by the Human Resources/Risk Management Division based on the City&rsquo;s organizational structure, operational alignment, and distribution of eligible employees.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Human Resources/Risk Management Division will assign groups using the following criteria:</p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The existing division structure will be considered, and division representation may be grouped based on functional or operational similarity of divisions or work units.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Reasonable balance of eligible employees to ensure equitable representation.</p>

            <p class="P2">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Organizational changes, such as restructuring, creation, or dissolution of divisions.</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The number of EAC members assigned to each group is based on the total number of tenured, tenure-eligible, and exempt employees within that group, as follows:</p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Groups with fewer than fifty (50) eligible employees are assigned one (1) regular member.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Groups with fifty (50) to one hundred (100) eligible employees are assigned two (2) regular members.</p>

            <p class="P2">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Groups with more than one hundred (100) eligible employees are assigned three (3) regular members.</p>

            <p class="P1">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;An equal number of alternate members will also be elected for each group.</p>

            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Human Resources/Risk Management Division will review group composition and member allocation at least annually, or more frequently as operational changes require.</p>

            <p class="P1">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Adjustments to representation will be made as follows:</p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the number of assigned members exceeds the appropriate count by the time of an election, positions will be reduced through natural term expirations or vacancies.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If fewer members exist than required, additional regular or alternate members will be elected to meet the appropriate representation level.</p>

            <p class="P1">E.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Regular members and alternate members will serve staggered three (3) year terms to ensure continuity. Alternate members are encouraged to attend all meetings and may vote when serving in place of a regular member.</p>

            <p class="P1">F.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The Human Resources/Risk Management Director, or designee, shall serve as a permanent, nonvoting member of the EAC to provide support and guidance. (Ord. 2010-33, Amended, 11/09/2010; Ord. 2014-32, Amended, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2020-23, Amended, 09/15/2020; Ord. 2022-15, Amended, 07/05/2022; Ord. 2025-05, Amended, 04/15/2025 (Res. 2025-17); Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.6"><a name="1.14.001.0006.6">1-14-001-0006.6</a> Elections and Membership</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;City-wide elections for membership shall be held annually in July, with terms beginning at the first meeting in August.</p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Eligible employees shall nominate regular members and alternate members within their respective group.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The eligible employee with the most votes becomes the regular member and the next highest will become the alternate member. Ties require a runoff election.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the total membership count for a group is below fifty percent (50%), a special election may be considered at any time by the Human Resources/Risk Management Director and co-chairs.</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Special elections will be conducted during the second meeting in August for the following positions:</p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Election of co-chairs when necessary.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Election of a member responsible for meeting minutes, with a backup and/or rotation as deemed necessary.</p>

            <p class="P2">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Election of one (1) member and one (1) alternate to represent EAC during budget meetings to present EAC budget priorities to the City Manager and City Council.</p>

            <p class="P2">4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Members may also be elected to serve on special committees or task forces.</p>

            <p class="P2">5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If an elected member or alternate cannot attend a committee meeting, the co-chair(s) may designate another member to attend.</p>

            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Newly elected regular members and alternate members shall attend an orientation with a co-chair and/or the Human Resources/Risk Management Director or designee between August and November. (Ord. 2009-10, Amended, 06/02/2009; Ord. 2010-33, Amended, 11/09/2010; Ord. 2014-32, Amended, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2020-23, Amended, 09/15/2020; Ord. 2025-05, Amended, 04/15/2025 (Res. 2025-17); Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.7"><a name="1.14.001.0006.7">1-14-001-0006.7</a> Resignation or Removal</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Members wishing to resign shall submit a written notice to the co-chairs and Human Resources/Risk Management Director.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When a regular member resigns, the alternate member with the corresponding term will complete the remaining term. If there is no alternate member with a corresponding term, the alternate member will finish out the remaining term.</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If a co-chair resigns, a special election shall be held to elect a replacement for the remainder of the term.</p>

            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Members with three (3) consecutive unexcused absences may be removed by a majority vote of the EAC.</p>

            <p class="P1">E.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Employees may request removal of a member representing their group through the following process:</p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Submit a written complaint explaining the reason for the request to remove the current EAC member to the Human Resources/Risk Management Director.</p>

            <p class="P3">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Only employees from that member&rsquo;s group may file the complaint.</p>

            <p class="P3">b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Human Resources/Risk Management will relay the complaint to the current co-chairs.</p>

            <p class="P3">c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The co-chairs will recuse themselves from the process if the complaint is about them or another member from their respective group.</p>

            <p class="P3">d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The co-chairs will speak with the member to obtain additional information about the complaint.</p>

            <p class="P3">e.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The co-chairs, with assistance from the Human Resources/Risk Management Director, will determine whether the complaint is substantiated.</p>

            <p class="P4">i.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If unsubstantiated, the co-chairs will notify the complainant.</p>

            <p class="P4">ii.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If substantiated, the process will continue.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The member will have a two (2) month period to address the area(s) of concern.</p>

            <p class="P2">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The co-chairs will follow up with the complainant to determine progress.</p>

            <p class="P3">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If satisfactory improvements are made, the complaint will be closed.</p>

            <p class="P3">b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If satisfactory improvements are not made, a second complaint will be filed by the co-chairs.</p>

            <p class="P2">4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon the second complaint, the co-chairs and Human Resources/Risk Management will hold a removal election.</p>

            <p class="P3">a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;At least fifty percent (50%) plus one (1) of the member&rsquo;s group must vote for the election to be valid.</p>

            <p class="P3">b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If turnout is insufficient, the member continues their term.</p>

            <p class="P3">c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If turnout is sufficient and the majority votes to retain, the member&rsquo;s term continues.</p>

            <p class="P3">d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If turnout is sufficient and the majority votes to remove, the member&rsquo;s term ends. The alternate member with the corresponding term as the outgoing member will serve the remaining term. If there is no alternate member with the corresponding term, an alternate member will be selected by EAC to serve the remaining term. (Ord. 2014-32, Enacted, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2020-23, Amended, 09/15/2020; Ord. 2025-05, Amended, 04/15/2025 (Res. 2025-17); Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.8"><a name="1.14.001.0006.8">1-14-001-0006.8</a> Meetings</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The EAC shall meet twice per month unless a majority vote approves a reduced frequency.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Special meetings may be called by the co-chair(s).</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Regular members must notify their alternate member(s) and co-chairs, in a timely manner, when they are unable to attend.</p>

            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Co-chairs may request a meeting with the City Manager as needed.</p>

            <p class="P1">E.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If an issue raised with the City Manager remains unresolved, the EAC may authorize a co-chair or designee to present the issue to City Council at a public meeting to review the issue, upon recommendation and majority vote of the EAC.</p>

            <p class="P1">F.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Recommendations require majority vote of the quorum (one (1) more than half of voting members).</p>

            <p class="P1">G.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All votes not unanimous shall result in a roll call vote and will be recorded into the meeting minutes.</p>

            <p class="P1">H.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;All employees may request an agenda item through any regular member.</p>

            <p class="P2">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Employees may request anonymity.</p>

            <p class="P2">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Employees will be notified by a co-chair of the meeting time and date; attendance at the meeting to discuss the agenda item proposed by the employee counts as hours worked.</p>

            <p class="P1">I.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The City Manager may contact a co-chair to place an item on the agenda. (Ord. 1738, Enacted, 06/09/92; Ord. 1982, Amended, 09/15/98; Ord. 2000-20, Amended, 09/05/2000; Ord. 2003-15, Repealed/Replaced, 09/16/2003; Ord. No. 2009-10 Repeal/Replaced, 06/02/2009; Ord. 2010-33, Amended, 11/09/2010; Ord. 2014-32, Amended, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38). Formerly 1-14-001-0006.7)</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.9"><a name="1.14.001.0006.9">1-14-001-0006.9</a> Notice and Procedure for Meetings</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Agendas must be posted at least twenty-four (24) hours before meetings on resources accessible to all employees.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Meeting minutes will be posted within five (5) calendar days after approval on resources accessible to all employees.</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The EAC may adopt additional procedures to govern its meetings. (Ord. 2014-32, Enacted, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2020-23, Amended, 09/15/2020; Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.10"><a name="1.14.001.0006.10">1-14-001-0006.10</a> Subcommittees</h3>
            <p class="P0">Subcommittees may be formed to address specific issues. They are encouraged to meet for one (1) hour, two (2) times per month. Each subcommittee dissolves when its assigned issue is resolved by vote of the full EAC. Subcommittees or the City Manager may invite nonmembers to participate. (Ord. 2014-32, Enacted, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="1.14.001.0006.11"><a name="1.14.001.0006.11">1-14-001-0006.11</a> Attendance and Hours Worked</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Members shall attend meetings using City time; such time counts as hours worked.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Nonmembers, including subcommittee members, may attend up to four (4) hours per month during regular working hours with written supervisor approval; such time counts as hours worked.</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Employees may attend EAC meetings during nonworking hours; such time does not count as hours worked.</p>

            <p class="P1">D.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The EAC may choose a member to attend portions of leadership or extended leadership meetings when EAC agenda items are discussed or upon request of the City Manager; such time counts as hours worked.</p>

            <p class="P1">E.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The EAC, City Manager, or Human Resources/Risk Management Director may invite any person to attend meetings; such time counts as hours worked. (Ord. 2014-32, Enacted, 01/06/2015; Ord. 2026-17, Amended, 07/07/2026 (Res. 2026-38))</p>

            <p class="P1"></p>

    </div>
